    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0576" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg478"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-14"><hi rendition="#italic">June 14,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 793.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is in receipt of a letter of
                    the 2d instant from the mayor of San Francisco, in which he states that on the
                    evening of the 25th ultimo a fire broke out on the harbor front of that city.
                    The French cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Protet</hi> lay in the harbor at that
                    time, and her captain, M. Germinet, sent on shore a part of her crew, who
                    volunteered their services and aided in extinguishing the flames.</p>
                <p>You are now instructed to convey to the French Government the thanks of the mayor
                    of San Francisco for this kind act of the commander and crew of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Protet.</hi></p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
